    narr:generatedFrom "6a9c720473f9540d5ad542f2925d90f61d74241f" ;
    narr:narration """This position holds that [reactions route through one bundle per run per person, not one message per skill](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2), restated as [a directive establishing reaction delivery policy](narr:Expr_3DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESyntheticAttempt2_2), and re-voiced again in [the same routing rule](narr:Expr_20260924_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_hf8fb95c0b315_2), [the ruling directive on bundling reaction delivery](narr:Expr_20260924_2_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESyntheticAttempt2_haec961429483_2), [a direct quote stating the routing rule](narr:Expr_20260926_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_ha66ee8b3c008_2), and [the same rule stated once more](narr:Expr_20260928_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h801a6165fef3_2). The window is bounded by [the bundle closing when the run closes, with a late skill waiting for the next run rather than sending on its own](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3), narrated in [the pushback and ruling on the batching window](narr:Expr_3DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESyntheticAttempt2_3), [the editorial narrative of the held position](narr:Expr_20260924_2_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESyntheticAttempt2_haec961429483_3), [the boundary held against pushback](narr:Expr_20260924_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_hf8fb95c0b315_3), [the summary of the pushback and its resolution](narr:Expr_20260926_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_ha66ee8b3c008_3), and [the boundary restated once more](narr:Expr_20260928_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h801a6165fef3_3). The boundary was chosen against [a rejected alternative of per-skill delivery with client-side collapsing](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4), reported again in [the rejected architectural alternative](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5), [the report of the rejected alternative](narr:Expr_3DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESyntheticAttempt2_4), [the editorial summary of the rejected alternative](narr:Expr_20260924_2_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESyntheticAttempt2_haec961429483_4), [the rejected alternative re-reported](narr:Expr_20260924_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_hf8fb95c0b315_4), [the summary of the rejected alternative](narr:Expr_20260926_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_ha66ee8b3c008_4), and [the alternative named once more](narr:Expr_20260928_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h801a6165fef3_4). The member expressions carry an antithesis-and-parallelism register — the ruling names what it is not before what it is.""" ;
    narr:reaction """Since the last review, the ruling repeats without change through [a further direct restatement of the routing rule](narr:Expr_20260926_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_ha66ee8b3c008_2) and [a still further restatement](narr:Expr_20260928_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h801a6165fef3_2), so the bundle-per-run boundary and the rejected per-skill alternative remain exactly as you read them before. The one new note: [the latest restatement of the routing rule](narr:Expr_20260928_1_DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_h801a6165fef3_2) softens the relational footing toward shared ground alongside authority, a register absent from the earlier restatements. Nothing else moved — the boundary, the pushback, and the rejected alternative hold exactly as narrated.""" ;
